Photorealistic vintage 1984 Japanese high-end audio cassette deck user-interface asset: one single wide horizontal push button plate, viewed perfectly straight-on, centered, spanning 88 percent of the image width and about one quarter of its height, isolated on a pure flat black background. Shape: long horizontal rectangular bar with finely chamfered precision-machined corners, like high-end Tokyo audiophile rack gear. Frame: thick brushed champagne-silver anodized aluminum bezel with subtle machined screw heads at the far left and far right ends. Face: completely blank smoked dark acrylic with a fine horizontal hairline brush, and a thin continuous glowing fluorescent teal VFD meter line recessed just inside the aluminum bezel. Studio product photography, crisp macro focus, perfectly symmetrical, even clean lighting. Absolutely no text, no letters, no symbols, no icons, no logos on the face. One object only, pure flat black background, no shadows on background, no watermark.
